# Issue #647 / roadmap 7.8 — project-level config for the shellcheck
# pre-commit hook (.pre-commit-config.yaml), so it gates real bugs without
# forcing an unrelated style rewrite of already-reviewed scripts.
#
# SC2129 (style: prefer `{ cmd1; cmd2; } >> file` over individual redirects)
# — deploy/install.sh's env-file writers mix a heredoc and printf appends
# deliberately (see that file's own PR #529 comments on why interpolated
# vs. printf-escaped content is split the way it is); a style rewrite here
# is out of scope for this feature and risks re-litigating already-reviewed
# hardening.
disable=SC2129
